  "notes": "{鳴|な}らす means to cause something to produce sound — to ring, sound, or play.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{鳴|な}る→鳴る：01143_naru⟧ (intransitive — the thing itself sounds)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{鳴|な}らしている means 'is ringing/sounding (something)' — an ongoing action.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦ベル→ベル：01379_beru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす: to ring a bell\n- ⟦{警報|けいほう}→警報：09515_keihou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす: to sound an alarm\n- ⟦クラクション→クラクション：27848_kurakushon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす: to honk a horn\n- ⟦{指|ゆび}→指：01518_yubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす: to snap one's fingers\n- ⟦{太鼓|たいこ}→太鼓：04049_taiko⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす: to beat a drum\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦{名|な}→名：03496_na⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鳴|な}らす means to make a name for oneself, to become famous.",
